# Port isolation

Scratch from the Fabric 26.2 port lives only under gitignored `.port/` at the repo root. Do not add port artifacts, test worlds, logs, experimental copies, extra folders, or throwaway scripts anywhere else.

## Put in `.port/`

- Compile/test logs, error dumps, comparison diffs
- Experimental copies of Gradle files or Java sources
- Test run directories, extra mods, jars, world saves
- Notes, checklists, and generated reports created during the port
- Any new top-level folder that is not already part of the fork

## Keep in the real tree

Intentional port edits to existing project files (`fabric/`, Gradle pins, mixins, compat plugins). Those are the update, not scratch.

## Do not

- Create `scratch/`, `tmp/`, `test/`, `_backup/`, or similar next to `common/`, `fabric/`, or `neoforge/`
- Commit `.port/` (it is gitignored)
- Copy port junk into `common/` or `neoforge/` "for later"
